<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monrovia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Monrovia is the capital of Liberia, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-mesurado">Cape Mesurado</a> at the mouth of the Saint Paul River. It was founded in 1822 by free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-americans">African Americans</a> settled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-colonization-society">American Colonization Society</a> and named in 1824 after President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-monroe">James Monroe</a>. It became the capital of the independent Republic of Liberia in 1847 and is the country's main port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monrovia.jpg" alt="Monrovia" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: blk24ga · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liberia,_Africa_-_panoramio_(256).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
